      },
      "cite": "eq-cofactor-expansion",
      "prompt": "<p>Compute determinant of $\\left[ \\begin{smallmatrix} 9 & -2 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 10 & -2 & -6 \\end{smallmatrix} \\right]$.</p>",
      "answer": {
        "type": "number",
        "generated_by": "ai",
        "value": 6,
        "solution": "Expand along the first row: $\\det = 9 \\det\\left[ \\begin{smallmatrix} 3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & -6 \\end{smallmatrix} \\right] - (-2)\\det\\left[ \\begin{smallmatrix} -8 & 6 \\\\ 10 & -6 \\end{smallmatrix} \\right] + (-6)\\det\\left[ \\begin{smallmatrix} -8 & 3 \\\\ 10 & -2 \\end{smallmatrix} \\right] = 9(-18+12) + 2(48-60) - 6(16-30) = -54 - 24 + 84 = 6$."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e4",
      "source_id": "3.2.4",
      "source_number": "3.2.4",
      "kind": "exercise",
      "bloom": "Apply",
      "place": {
        "at": "end"
      },
      "cite": "cofactors",
      "prompt": "<p>Compute determinant of $\\left[ \\begin{smallmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 10 & 1 \\end{smallmatrix} \\right]$. Hint: Expand along the proper row or column to make the calculations simpler.</p>",
      "answer": {
        "type": "number",
        "generated_by": "ai",
        "value": 4,
        "solution": "The second column has only one nonzero entry, $a_{12} = 2$, so expanding along it leaves one term: $\\det = {(-1)}^{1+2} \\cdot 2 \\det\\left[ \\begin{smallmatrix} 4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 10 & 1 \\end{smallmatrix} \\right]$. In that $3 \\times 3$ matrix the third column has only the entry $1$ in the corner, so its determinant is ${(-1)}^{3+3} \\cdot 1 \\cdot \\det\\left[ \\begin{smallmatrix} 4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 7 \\end{smallmatrix} \\right] = 28 - 30 = -2$. Hence $\\det = -2 \\cdot (-2) = 4$."
      }
    },
