      "cite": "thm-3-2-1",
      "prompt": "<p>For which $h$ is $\\left[ \\begin{smallmatrix} h & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & h & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & h \\end{smallmatrix} \\right]$ not invertible? Find all such $h$.</p>",
      "answer": {
        "type": "open",
        "generated_by": "ai",
        "solution": "$h = -1$, $h = 0$ and $h = 1$. The second row has the single nonzero entry $h$, so expanding along it, $\\det = {(-1)}^{2+2} h \\det\\left[ \\begin{smallmatrix} h & 1 \\\\ 1 & h \\end{smallmatrix} \\right] = h(h^2 - 1) = h(h-1)(h+1)$. By Theorem 3.2.1 the matrix is not invertible exactly when this is zero, which happens for $h = 0$, $h = 1$ and $h = -1$."
      }
