            "value": 2.5
          }
        ],
        "solution": "$\\kvecx = \\left[ \\begin{smallmatrix} 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5/2 \\end{smallmatrix} \\right]$. The determinant is $6$ (Exercise 3.2.3), so the solution is unique. Row reducing the augmented matrix $\\left[ \\begin{smallmatrix} 9 & -2 & -6 & | & 1 \\\\ -8 & 3 & 6 & | & 2 \\\\ 10 & -2 & -6 & | & 3 \\end{smallmatrix} \\right]$ (subtract the first row from the third to get $[\\,1 ~~ 0 ~~ 0 ~|~ 2\\,]$, so $\\kxone = 2$; then the first two rows give $-2\\kxtwo - 6\\kxthree = -17$ and $3\\kxtwo + 6\\kxthree = 18$, whose sum is $\\kxtwo = 1$, and so $6\\kxthree = 15$) gives $\\kxone = 2$, $\\kxtwo = 1$, $\\kxthree = \\frac{5}{2}$. Check: $18 - 2 - 15 = 1$, $-16 + 3 + 15 = 2$, $20 - 2 - 15 = 3$."
      }
